Cloud computing is the on-demand delivery of IT resources—such as servers, storage, databases, and software—over the internet with pay-as-you-go pricing, rather than owning and maintaining physical data centers. It enables companies to lower costs, scale infrastructure instantly, and access services from providers like AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud.
